     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Only the masculine changes",
     "texto": [
      "Compare: **Der Koffer, der neu ist** (subject: nominative) versus **Der Koffer, den ich gekauft habe** (direct object: accusative; the subject is «ich»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The verb still goes at the end",
     "texto": [
      "In compound tenses such as the Perfekt, the auxiliary verb («habe / bin») goes at the very end after the participle: **Das Hotel, das ich gebucht habe**."
